{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderEdgeSuppression","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderEdgeSuppression","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barOdd_ratio_exceeded_of_not_edge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barOdd_ratio_exceeded_of_not_edge","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderEdgeSuppression.lean#L91-L101","doc":"**Falsifiable converse — the substrate↔fibre transition criterion.** If the\nleast term is *not* at the edge (some `k ≤ n` has `c k x^k < c n x^n`), then a\nrung-ratio radius was exceeded: `∃ k < n, c k < c (k+1) · x`. Crossing a rung\nradius is exactly the fibre transition where the least term leaves the top and\nthe Stokes datum turns on (corpus threshold `r* = |d₃₀/d₃₁|`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barOdd_leastTerm_at_edge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barOdd_leastTerm_at_edge","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderEdgeSuppression.lean#L59-L89","doc":"**Anchor-blindness / least-term-at-edge.** If the argument `x ≥ 0` lies below\nevery rung-ratio radius on `[0, n)` (`c (k+1) · x ≤ c k` for all `k < n`), then\nthe power-magnitude sequence `t_k = c_k x^k` is antitone on `[0, n]` and attains\nits minimum at the **edge index `n`**: `c n x^n ≤ c k x^k` for every `k ≤ n`.\n\nPhysical content: at the substrate `ũ₀`, the least term (the Stokes ambiguity\n`δ_np`) is the *top* rung of the ladder — exponentially suppressed — so the\nresummed value is anchor-blind. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barOdd_term_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barOdd_term_step","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderEdgeSuppression.lean#L48-L57","doc":"One rung step: if `x` is at or below the local ratio radius `c k / c (k+1)`\n(equivalently `c (k+1) · x ≤ c k`) and `x ≥ 0`, then the term magnitude does\nnot increase from index `k` to `k+1`: `c (k+1) x^{k+1} ≤ c k x^k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}